reviewer_concerns.value:
The reviewers initially raised several key concerns: 

(1) insufficient statistical validation of the core claim that low saliency correlates with hallucinations, relying only on illustrative cases; 

(2) marginal performance gains in Table 1 possibly falling within experimental noise; 

(3) a large number of hyperparameters without thorough sensitivity analysis; 

(4) lack of causal evidence linking saliency to hallucination.
